  "body": "**Link to problem area**:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec/blob/main/data/api/client-server/capabilities.yaml#L46\r\n\r\nhttps://spec.matrix.org/v1.11/client-server-api/#capabilities-negotiation\r\n\r\n![Screenshot 2024-09-09 at 10 57 59](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a1f5ad6c-62db-401d-8ec5-3c8bd025a706)\r\n\r\n**Issue**\r\n\r\nSimilar to https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec/issues/1913, the spec currently restricts custom capabilities to object types. This rules out potentially viable other types such as booleans or arrays.\r\n\r\nThe original [MSC](https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/1753/files#diff-64defa705e0c3cdc56f8b457ea856bce3d077cc750d2a39f389be8decb10b80dR33-R34) doesn't appear to specify any type restriction for individual capabilities. Therefore, I suspect this got added to the spec accidentally.",
